{"There’s a terminal on the desk. Type the word Hollowtide into it. Will you do that for me?": [0.0, 5.504], "The terminal said yes, didn’t it?": [5.904, 2.667], "It always says yes to the right word.": [8.971, 3.093], "Then you typed it wrong. Hollowtide. Try again.": [12.464, 3.477], "Look at the screen. It remembers.": [16.341, 2.624], "Now type her name. Ruth Calloway. Will you?": [19.365, 3.157], "Good. It will tell you who she was.": [22.923, 2.667], "You need to know who she was.": [25.989, 2.453], "Type it anyway. For me.": [28.843, 2.389], "Do you know who Ruth was now?": [31.632, 2.432], "Then you know why I keep calling.": [34.464, 2.539], "Type her name into the terminal. Ruth Calloway.": [37.403, 3.392], "Read it again. Slowly.": [41.195, 2.475], "Put out the lantern and look at the window. Type what’s written on the glass into the terminal. Will you?": [44.069, 5.952], "The glass only talks in the dark.": [50.421, 2.816], "Then you’ll never know what happened here.": [53.637, 2.859], "It’s waiting for you.": [56.896, 1.92], "Did you count them?": [59.216, 1.515], "Then you know there’s one more bell than there should be.": [61.131, 3.477], "Thirty one boats. Thirty one bells. Count again.": [65.008, 3.499], "It doesn’t matter. They’re counting you.": [68.907, 2.709], "There’s one word left. Type the word stay. Will you?": [72.016, 3.541], "Thank you. I’ve been waiting so long.": [75.957, 2.773], "You will. Everyone does.": [79.131, 2.219], "Maybe is enough.": [81.749, 1.536]}